  message: "PR #2354 (stable-id v19, 2026-11-23/24) re-measured two of this item's bullets on other trees; nothing here was fixed by it.\n- Forward declarations: a C++ `class X;` is emitted as a class beside its definition, at namespace/file scope as well as nested. After the PR's C/C++ guard and locals fixes, the pre-split stable-id ties left on libzmq are 14 groups, 12 of them class forward declarations (socket_base_t in src/proxy.cpp lines 21-23, 215-218, 486-489, src/proxy.hpp 8-15; session_base_t, io_thread_t, ctx_t, pipe_t, trie_t ...); on zstd 1 of 3 (contrib/pzstd/utils/ResourcePool.h Deleter [33, 79]). Guards agent, ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/guards/measure/zmq_ties.txt, zstd_ties_fixed.txt.\n- Template specialisation members: explicit-specialisation members tie in the stable id (their scope label lacks the specialisation's arguments). C++ fixture ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v19_11232026/guards/finam_fixture/b.cpp (`template <> struct Tp<int>`); CUDA, whisper.cpp ggml-cuda: pre-split ties 15 -> 8 after the CUDA guard fix, the 8 left are members of template specialisations (get_alpha x3). Guards agent, guards/RESULTS.md \"Follow-up\" and \"Follow-up 3\".\n- Same-line overload node ids: the PR's @<column> suffix (FileAnalysis.add_symbol) is used by Swift, Nix and Vue only; cpp.py registers symbols by hand, so this item's \"node ids collide for same-name overloads declared on one line\" stands. Filed as a cross-analyzer item: WI-jizus-gahoh-dazaz-lasul-bilun-sizup-havah-takin.\nFixing the first two moves C++ (and CUDA) stable ids: next scheme bump."  # aa66
